This package includes a pure-R implementation of the encoding-repair design and
character tables derived from [ftfy 6.3.1](https://github.com/rspeer/python-ftfy)
by [Robyn Speer](https://github.com/rspeer).  The relevant parts follow the
Apache License, Version 2.0, available at:

https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The surrounding lupa package is distributed under GPL-3.  ftfy 6.3.1 does not
include a NOTICE file; consequently there is no additional NOTICE attribution
to reproduce here.  No ftfy source code is bundled: the implementation in lupa
was written independently from the published design. The package does
redistribute literal data dumps of ftfy's character tables, badness categories
and regular expressions as fixtures; these are data, not source code, and are
distributed under the same Apache-2.0 terms.

The package also redistributes the frozen sentinel values from [naniar
1.1.0](https://github.com/njtierney/naniar), an MIT-licensed package by
[Nicholas Tierney](https://github.com/njtierney), [Di Cook](https://github.com/dicook),
[Miles McBain](https://github.com/milesmcbain), [Colin Fay](https://github.com/ColinFay)
and contributors. Copyright (c) Nicholas Tierney, Di Cook, Miles McBain, Colin
Fay and contributors. The
copyright and license notice for that package is available in its
[LICENSE](https://github.com/njtierney/naniar/blob/main/LICENSE).
